Z||000045||The Fieromaster||11-25-2001||09:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierochild:<BR><B>Thanks Tiger!<BR>     Love the sig.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  The color is original custom.  I spotted the color on the Interstate Batteries race car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> in a Nascar calender.  I took the page to Maco and told the painter to match it.  He did.  Turns out (due to printing ink) to be a shade different.  It sure turns heads everywhere I go.  I've tried to post other pics on the forum with out success.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  Using PIP to upload to fiero.nl/uploads.  PIP says upload successful.  I loading photos from my documents.  Does PIP automatically add this extention to the upload location?  Wouldn"t life be great without computer illiterates like me.  Anyway, thanks again for the sig.  At least I'll be able to show people what my car looks like.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OK here goes... how to work PIP easiest... <BR>After you get the upload complete and click OK.. click HISTORY on the side panel... Find the pic you wanna post and click it ONCE then in the boottom text box the COMPLETE code will appear!! Double click the code and then hit CTRL (control) and C (that will copy the code!) then in your post hit CTRL V (that will paste the code!  Then BOOM your done!<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">    <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
